WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:03.778
- Imagine instead of white,
gray, or black rooftops

00:00:03.778 --> 00:00:06.172
you look out over a sea of green

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:07.714
that stretches to the horizon.

00:00:07.714 --> 00:00:11.569
That's really what our
vision looks like long term.

00:00:11.569 --> 00:00:14.195
We're Up Top Acres and
we grow food on roofs.

00:00:14.195 --> 00:00:16.159
We convert underutilized spaces

00:00:16.159 --> 00:00:18.431
into vibrant productive farmland and

00:00:18.431 --> 00:00:20.530
we use this farmland to try to drive

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:23.240
the conversation to create better cities.

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:24.891
To turn them from concrete jungles

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:27.269
into living, breathing ecosystems.

00:00:27.269 --> 00:00:30.291
- 80% of the US population
lives in cities right now,

00:00:30.291 --> 00:00:33.479
and we are shipping food 1,500 miles

00:00:33.479 --> 00:00:35.052
on average from farm to table.

00:00:35.052 --> 00:00:36.835
- So instead of miles driven we're

00:00:36.835 --> 00:00:39.585
trying to measure the
distance our produce travels

00:00:39.585 --> 00:00:40.698
in flights of stairs.

00:00:40.698 --> 00:00:43.900
- It's a lot more than
just growing food on roofs.

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:47.553
It's also about how can we create the city

00:00:47.553 --> 00:00:50.520
of the future and to
make it a reality now.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:54.073
The end goal is really just
to create a better city.

00:00:54.073 --> 00:00:56.414
This year we're shooting to have about 70%

00:00:56.414 --> 00:00:58.897
of produce grown on the roofs distributed

00:00:58.897 --> 00:01:01.268
to the buildings that
those farms are on top of.

00:01:01.268 --> 00:01:04.689
And then the other 30% will go to

00:01:04.689 --> 00:01:07.217
the farmers market and
then also some restaurants

00:01:07.217 --> 00:01:08.884
in the neighborhood.

00:01:23.621 --> 00:01:26.456
I wanted to start Up Top Acres

00:01:26.456 --> 00:01:29.081
because I wanted to combine the two things

00:01:29.081 --> 00:01:31.495
that I really like which is farming

00:01:31.495 --> 00:01:33.317
and living in the city and I think

00:01:33.317 --> 00:01:34.421
that all three of us deep down

00:01:34.421 --> 00:01:36.696
really wanted to try to make our city

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:37.622
that we grew up in,

00:01:37.622 --> 00:01:39.702
that we love truly a better place.

00:01:39.702 --> 00:01:42.518
We're going to deliver to a market cafe

00:01:42.518 --> 00:01:44.062
called Little Red Fox.

00:01:44.062 --> 00:01:48.229
They're some of our oldest
clients and we love them.

00:01:50.676 --> 00:01:52.165
- Up Top Acres is one of the local vendors

00:01:52.165 --> 00:01:53.110
that we work with.

00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:55.472
Having ultra fresh produce
is a lot more exciting

00:01:55.472 --> 00:01:57.185
for the customers just to be able

00:01:57.185 --> 00:01:59.165
to know that this was grown downtown

00:01:59.165 --> 00:02:01.616
and got delivered this morning.

00:02:01.616 --> 00:02:03.703
So we're here on harvest day and we're

00:02:03.703 --> 00:02:06.975
about to harvest some of
our all star lettuce mix.

00:02:06.975 --> 00:02:09.616
And it's gonna be distributed
to our CSA members

00:02:09.616 --> 00:02:13.449
down in the lobby of the
building later today.

00:02:33.626 --> 00:02:34.741
- I'm gonna go cook.

00:02:34.741 --> 00:02:36.383
- See ya, enjoy!
- Thank you!

00:02:36.383 --> 00:02:39.447
- Everyone benefits when
we're installing the system.

00:02:39.447 --> 00:02:40.745
You're reducing energy cost,

00:02:40.745 --> 00:02:42.331
you're reducing storm water runoff,

00:02:42.331 --> 00:02:44.397
you have access to fresh food and

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:46.859
it's a benefit for the
surrounding community

00:02:46.859 --> 00:02:49.771
because these are unique natural spaces

00:02:49.771 --> 00:02:51.869
that don't usually exist in cities

00:02:51.869 --> 00:02:55.369
but we're right on top of a metro station.

00:03:07.334 --> 00:03:08.868
One of the biggest things
that sticks with me

00:03:08.868 --> 00:03:11.149
is whenever anyone comes up onto the roof

00:03:11.149 --> 00:03:13.434
they always shave the
same sort of reaction.

00:03:13.434 --> 00:03:16.346
It's why isn't this being
done on every building?

00:03:16.346 --> 00:03:19.039
When I hear that that's
really what drives me

00:03:19.039 --> 00:03:20.884
is let's make this a reality on every

00:03:20.884 --> 00:03:23.801
new building that we're putting up.

